{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>and do not</b> — The custom of passersby is to say to the reapers: 'HaShem bless you with what He has given you.' The meaning: since people will not praise [one] for his Torah and faith — for there is no faith in their hearts — therefore he likened Israel, keepers of the Torah, to sowers, and the nations of the lands who guard their vanities, he likened to grass on housetops."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 129, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:26.807165382Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}